            ["<b>Shareholders' equity</b>", "The amount contributed to the financing of the company by shareholders over time, by <b>one of two means</b>: <b>first</b>, shareholders might have contributed by <b>buying shares from the company when they were first issued — that is, in the primary market</b>, which is the amount in the <b>common shares</b> account; <b>second</b>, all the company's <b>annual profits that have not been distributed to shareholders (generally as dividends) but reinvested in the company</b> continue to accumulate as <b>retained earnings</b>. <b>The decision to reinvest comes from the company's board of directors.</b>"]
